1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:03,180
What if your skin could make food from sunlight, like a leaf?

2
00:00:03,683 --> 00:00:05,154
First, you'd turn green.

3
00:00:05,154 --> 00:00:09,566
Chlorophyll uses less of the green light, so green is what bounces back.

4
00:00:10,050 --> 00:00:14,039
At noon, sunlight brings about a thousand watts to every square meter.

5
00:00:14,039 --> 00:00:16,717
But plants only store around one percent of it.

6
00:00:17,217 --> 00:00:20,391
For you, that's about one percent of your daily energy.

7
00:00:20,391 --> 00:00:21,777
Roughly a cracker a day.

8
00:00:21,777 --> 00:00:25,644
To live on sunlight alone, you'd need about a tennis court of skin.

9
00:00:26,150 --> 00:00:29,241
Your brain alone burns about twenty percent of your energy.

10
00:00:29,750 --> 00:00:31,713
So how do some animals pull it off?

11
00:00:31,713 --> 00:00:33,171
Full story on the channel.
